    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize learning by adapting explanations to individual strengths/weaknesses. They’d bridge gaps for students like me who struggle with abstract concepts but excel in applied problem-solving. Interactive exercises, real-time feedback, and conceptual scaffolding would make math less intimidating while maintaining rigor."
